%% Source: the README write-protection encryption diagram + docs/diagrams/encryption.png.
%% Re-render command (from repo root): npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i docs/diagrams/encryption.mmd -o docs/diagrams/encryption.png -c docs/diagrams/mermaid-config.json -b white -s 2
%% Reference: see the header comment in lib/shared/crypto.ts — the master key never goes into the database, git, or an echoed response; read endpoints only ever return a masked value; encryption and decryption use the same key.
%% Block grid approach (in a flowchart, two nodes with no incoming edges get stacked vertically instead of laid out in a row, so a block grid is used to lock the layout).
block-beta
  columns 2
  IN["Sensitive value<br/>e.g. LLM key"] K["Master key<br/>env var only"]
  E["Server-side encryption<br/>AES-256-GCM"] DB["app_config table<br/>ciphertext only"]
  D["Decrypted server-side on use<br/>read endpoints return a masked value only"]:2
  IN --> E
  K --> E
  E --> DB
  DB --> D
